module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.type_name_field_carries_rendered_value

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data type_name_field_carries_rendered_value: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "type_name_field_carries_rendered_value" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a field named `type_name` holds a type name on three arms and a fully rendered value on the fourth** (INVALID STATE: `ExitClass::NotProcessExit { type_name }` is one spelling. `classify_exit` Variant arms that are not `ProcessExit` put `ctx.resolve(*type_name)` or `ProcessExit::<variant>` into it — an actual type or variant name. The final `other` arm puts `ctx.format_value(other)` — the rendered value — into the same field. `exit_status_for_class` interpolates that field into `returned `{type_name}`` with no second match, so every refusal path reads one name for two facts. HARM: a reader of the interpolation site infers the field's contents from its NAME and concludes a String projector yields the word String; a reader of the producer and a live stderr file concludes the markdown body is in the diagnostic. Both readings of adjacent code are correct; the name is a third surface and it lied. ",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-09-06, three conclusions from two lanes and their manager on the same function in twenty minutes. clever-otter-298 read `exit_status_for_class` and the enrolled control `non_process_exit_refuses_rather_than_printing_and_succeeding` (which constructs `NotProcessExit` with a fixture type_name Bool and never goes through `classify_exit`) and asserted the diagnostic names the type. wise-badger-902 read the same interpolation and relayed that a String projector yields the word String. quick-heron-85 held proj3.err at 1062137 bytes opening with expected_design_failure_modes_md returned the markdown heading and closing with not ProcessExit — they extracted between those delimiters. The manager then read `classify_exit`'s final arm and retracted. ",

    "THIS IS NOT `docs_markdown_projections_have_no_completing_actuator`. That row is the absence of a ProcessExit actuator and a content gate over generated `docs/*.md`. This row is a meaning fork inside `ExitClass`, reachable with no docs file in sight. Neighbour `meaning_fork` is the generic class; this instance is filed because the fork sat in the struct every refusal path reads and produced the three-way contradiction. Neighbour `diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent` is a diagnostic NAME silent about its predicate; here the FIELD name is accurate for three arms and false for the fourth. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a field is named for a kind of contents, read every constructor, not the interpolation site. If one constructor writes a different kind, the name has forked. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable — the wrong inference is a human reading; the runtime still refuses with exit 2 and does not print-and-succeed. CEILING: structurally impossible when `NotProcessExit` cannot be constructed with a rendered value under a field named for a type — two variants, or a field named for what it actually holds. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability: `ExitClass` distinguishes a type-name refusal from a rendered-value refusal in the type, so interpolating one as the other will not compile.)",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "classify_exit", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "exit_status_for_class", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
